nat44-ei: translate inside traffic after ABF and dns-intercept

On an inside interface the in2out features ran before abf-input-ip4 (and
dns-intercept-ip4, which runs just before ABF). With the router's LAN set as
inside, beside the output feature on the WAN, the source was already the
outside address when an ABF policy matched on the LAN prefix: Gate's DNS
hijack (an ACL on the LAN prefix, redirecting to vpp-host) stopped
matching, and LAN DNS went straight to the public resolver, bypassing Gate,
with no visible error.

Order nat44-ei-in2out, nat44-ei-in2out-worker-handoff, nat44-ei-classify
and nat44-ei-handoff-classify after both. Traffic an ABF policy redirects
then leaves the arc untranslated, as it does today with the output feature
alone; the rest is translated as before. Out2in is unchanged. The names
are only ordering constraints and need neither plugin loaded.

Verified in an isolated VPP (in/out, output feature, and output feature plus
inside interface): a redirected query reaches its ABF next hop from the
client's own address; without this patch, with an inside interface, it
leaves through the outside interface translated. On the test router with the
LAN as inside, the hijacked DNS reached Gate from the client again. Test:
tests/integration/integration_nat44_partial_checksum.py --nat ei.

--- a/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ei/nat44_ei.c
+++ b/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ei/nat44_ei.c
@@ -73,19 +73,25 @@
   .arc_name = "ip4-unicast",
   .node_name = "nat44-ei-classify",
   .runs_after = VNET_FEATURES ("acl-plugin-in-ip4-fa",
-			       "ip4-sv-reassembly-feature"),
+			       "ip4-sv-reassembly-feature",
+			       "dns-intercept-ip4",
+			       "abf-input-ip4"),
 };
 VNET_FEATURE_INIT (ip4_nat_handoff_classify, static) = {
   .arc_name = "ip4-unicast",
   .node_name = "nat44-ei-handoff-classify",
   .runs_after = VNET_FEATURES ("acl-plugin-in-ip4-fa",
-			       "ip4-sv-reassembly-feature"),
+			       "ip4-sv-reassembly-feature",
+			       "dns-intercept-ip4",
+			       "abf-input-ip4"),
 };
 VNET_FEATURE_INIT (ip4_nat44_ei_in2out, static) = {
